check_gram_chunk_count_is_pinned OK [FAST]: k partitions into 1728 chunks, and the workspace-sizing predicate independently implies the same 1728 (pinned constant is 128; under FAST this number is the machine's own and under IDENTICAL it is the constant)
check_gram_arm_is_pinned OK [FAST]: nvidia/amd rows answer False and bit-identical answers True; this build's arm compiles against column nvidia, which takes the split-K kernel at 32x32x4M: False and at 128-square: False. A False there is not a bug -- it is the FAST dispatch handing the Gram shape to linalg.matmul, and it is exactly what DEVIATION 521 stops an IDENTICAL build from doing.
check_gemm_tn_refuses_over_capacity OK [FAST]: 256x256x512 still runs on the transpose+matmul arm
check_pinned_gemm_is_batch_invariant REPORT [FAST]: 256 overlapping cells on the vendor matmul, n=4 as the reference -- n=64 differs in 234 cells, n=256 differs in 229. A nonzero count here is not a bug, it is the measurement that prices the pin: it means the shipped arm's answer for a row depends on how many other rows were in the launch.
